On 02/21/2013 06:06 PM, Finn Lindgren wrote:
> Actually, having tested this I realise that either there is a misprint in Cameletti or you skipped a step, since supplying coordinates in a data frame is not supported; it should be a matrix.  But in my testing with a data.frame, I get the error message _before_ seeing any triangulation progress, so this may be a separate issue.

Strange, I am checking this once again and  it is indeed a data frame.
You can see here http://www.math.ntnu.no/inla/r-inla.org/case-studies/Cameletti2012/run_model.R
that borders are obtained by the following:
borders <-read.table("Piemonte_borders.csv",header=TRUE,sep=",")

and read.table always reads a file in table format and creates a data frame from it.
So now I obtain a matrix and plug it in as a points domain.

borders<-borders.shp@polygons[[1]]@Polygons[[1]]@coords

After all, I manage to obtain a mesh (which still needs to be fine-tuned) and it works both on data frame and matrix.

